-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the smooth-point package on the supersingular component
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q \ge 5$, a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ — the subfield of $\kappa$-Laurent series generated by the two $j$-series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'` — with `hW` saying that membership in $W$ is membership in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, so that the elements of $W$ are exactly the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w(\,$`jGeomGen κ M'`$\,) \in$ `ssJSet q κ`; let $s$ be one of them. Let `hle` be the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ function field, into `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the function field of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring of the source contracting to $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which extends the reduction $A \to \kappa$, together with a normalisation clause, a map on places preserving degrees, and compatibility of divisor pushforward with orders of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that $R_0$ compute coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0$`.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, equals the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap (residue A) y`.
--
--   Further data: a field $F_{SS}$ which is an algebra over $\kappa$; a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{SS}$, that is a valuation subring $R$`.integers` of `fieldBar q M'` contracting to $A$ along $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, with a surjective residue map onto $F_{SS}$ whose kernel is its maximal ideal, extending $A \to \kappa$, and satisfying the normalisation clause that every non-zero element becomes, after scaling by a constant, an integer with non-zero residue; a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$; and, indexed by the places $Q$ of $F_{SS}$ over $\kappa$, a subring $S_Q =$ `Sx Q` of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q\colon A[T] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q}\colon S_Q \to \kappa$, and a set $D_Q =$ `Dx Q` of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are: `h0`, that $F_{SS}$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$; `h1`, that $R$ lies over $s$, namely for every $f \in R_0$`.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the order of the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb` is non-negative, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R$`.integers` and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{SS}$ of $s(R_0\text{-residue of } f)$, the value of $s$ at that residue; `h2`, that $R$`.integers` is invariant under the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hcard`, that $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   The hypothesis `hpkg` attaches to every place $Q \notin N$ the following fourteen clauses for the quadruple $(S_Q, \varphi_Q, \chi_{0,Q}, D_Q)$: the images of the elements of $A$ lie in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ in `fieldBar q M'` for every $a \in A$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the reduction of $a$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; for every $c \in A$ with zero reduction there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q \to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a$, with reduction of $\chi$ equal to $\chi_{0,Q}$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(T)) = c$; every $f \in S_Q$ lies in $R$`.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there of that $R$-residue is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; $\varphi_Q(T)$ lies in $R$`.integers` and its $R$-residue has order $1$ at $Q$; a place $P$ belongs to $D_Q$ precisely when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_Q$ one has $|P(f)| < 1$ in the valuation of $A$ if and only if $\chi_{0,Q}(f) = 0$; for every ring homomorphism $\chi\colon S_Q \to A$ splitting the constants and reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ there is a unique $P \in D_Q$ with $P(f) = \chi(f)$ for all $f \in S_Q$; for $P \in D_Q$, an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_Q$ with $P(h) \neq 0$; every non-zero $f$ of order $0$ at all $P \in D_Q$ satisfies $c f = u$ for some non-zero constant $c \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and some unit $u$ of $S_Q$; and every $f \in R$`.integers` lying in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   Three further hypotheses concern the family of discs: `hdisj`, that for $Q, Q' \notin N$ a common member of $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ forces $Q = Q'$; `hcusp`, that for $Q \notin N$ every $P \in D_Q$ gives non-negative order to the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $j$-series `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`; and `heqv`, that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism group of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $\tau$ preserving $R$`.integers`, with `R.resAut τ` the induced $\kappa$-automorphism of $F_{SS}$: a place $Q$ lies in $N$ if and only if `R.resAut τ • Q` does, and for $Q \notin N$ the transported disc `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Dx Q)`, namely $\{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q\}$, equals $D_{\,\mathtt{R.resAut τ}\, \cdot\, Q}$.
--
--   The conclusion is a uniqueness statement: for every place $Q \notin N$ and every quadruple consisting of a subring $S$ of `fieldBar q M'`, ring homomorphisms $\varphi\colon A[T] \to S$ and $\chi_0\colon S \to \kappa$, and a set $D$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, satisfying at $Q$ the same fourteen clauses as above (constants in $S$; $\varphi$ formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi$ on constants; $\chi_0 \circ \varphi$ on constants and at $T$; unique Hensel section for each $c$ with zero reduction; $R$ reading $\chi_0$ at $Q$; $\varphi(T)$ of order $1$ at $Q$; the characterisation of $D$; the bijection between sections and points of $D$; the description of the valuation subrings of points of $D$ as localisations of $S$; the unit principle; and saturation of $S$), the following three assertions hold: $D$ and $D_Q$ have the same members; $S$ and $S_Q$ have the same elements; and for every $f$ lying in both $S$ and $S_Q$ the values $\chi_0(f)$ and $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ agree in $\kappa$.
--
--   A rigidity statement for the local data at a smooth point of the supersingular fibre: the subring, the residue character and the residue disc of a smooth-point package over a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to the full level-$q^2M'$ function field are determined by the pair $(R, Q)$. It makes constructions that are phrased in terms of an arbitrary witness of the corresponding existence statement well posed in the tokens $S_Q$, $\chi_{0,Q}$, $D_Q$, and it is used in the assembly of the supersingular charts, node presentations, crossing units, Igusa data, inertia action and Hasse invariant for the full-level curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_supersingularProlongation_smoothPointPackage_unique.lean

